  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🛡️ Valkyrie Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Valkyrie names built from real Old Norse name parts, with a title to ride into battle with."
    },
    "intro": "Valkyries are the choosers of the slain in Norse myth, who carried fallen warriors to Valhalla. Their names were built from Old Norse words for battle, spears and shields. This **valkyrie name generator** builds names the same way, from real Old Norse name parts, with a title if you want one.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What a valkyrie is",
        "content": "<p>Valkyrie comes from the Old Norse <em>valkyrja</em>, \"chooser of the slain\": the women who served Odin and chose which warriors would die in battle.</p><ul><li><strong>Valhalla:</strong> the chosen dead were carried to Odin's hall, Valhalla, to feast and fight until the end of the world.</li><li><strong>Real names:</strong> Norse poems list valkyries by name, such as Hildr (\"battle\"), Þrúðr (\"strength\") and Skǫgul. The names are warlike because the valkyries were.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How valkyrie names are built",
        "content": "<p>Old Norse names, valkyries' included, were usually made of two parts, and the generator joins real ones.</p><ul><li><strong>Sig-</strong> means victory, <strong>Geir-</strong> spear, <strong>Hjor-</strong> sword and <strong>Bryn-</strong> mail armour.</li><li><strong>Rand-</strong> is the rim of a shield, <strong>Gunn-</strong> means war, <strong>Hild-</strong> battle and <strong>Val-</strong> the slain.</li><li><strong>Svan-</strong> means swan, <strong>Hrafn-</strong> raven and <strong>Ulf-</strong> wolf.</li><li><strong>Endings</strong> include <strong>-hild</strong> (battle), <strong>-run</strong> (secret, or rune) and <strong>-dis</strong> (goddess, or lady).</li></ul><p>So Sigrun is \"victory secret\" and Ulfdis \"wolf lady\". For more Norse names, try the <a href=\"viking-name-generator.html\">Viking</a> and <a href=\"nord-name-generator.html\">Nord</a> name generators.</p><p>For more gods and legends, see all the <a href=\"../categories/mythology-names.html\">mythology name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What does valkyrie mean?",
        "answer": "Chooser of the slain, from the Old Norse valkyrja: val (the slain) and kjósa (to choose)."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are some real valkyrie names?",
        "answer": "Norse poems name valkyries such as Hildr, Þrúðr, Skǫgul and Göndul. This generator builds new names from the same kind of parts."
      },
      {
        "question": "What does sig mean in Norse names?",
        "answer": "Victory. It's in names like Sigrun and Sigrid."
      }
    ]
  }
